Windows App SDK 2.5.1 (WinUI 3): Microsoft Software License Terms, © Microsoft Corporation.

Win2D 1.4.0: Microsoft license terms, © Microsoft Corporation.

The components' license texts come with their own packages.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_Terms_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Terms of use</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_Terms_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value># No warranty
Vacuo is provided "as is", with no warranty that it works, suits a purpose or is free of errors. The developer cannot be held liable for what comes of using it.

# Vacuo does nothing on its own
Moving files, tidying folders, closing or uninstalling programs only happen when you choose and confirm them.

# What can be undone
Everything moved goes to the Recycle Bin and can be put back from the Journal. Vacuo never empties the Recycle Bin; once it is emptied, those items cannot be brought back.

# What cannot be undone
Clean-ups done with administrator permission on the Windows screen are permanent. An uninstalled program only comes back by installing it again; the program's own uninstaller does the removal.

# Backups
Keeping backups of your important files is up to you.</value>
  </data>
